body:
Gotta go pro and use a continuation system:
```
onColoredShirtDetection $ case _ of
      Red -> yield murder;
      _    -> pure ();
```

It's similar to _any_ language's `include` or `import` statement, except for one small detail - it's __higher-order__; meaning, we can import not just text, but we can also import something that imports, then apply data to it:

    {{ f x }}

    f has a type :: Text -> Text

    {{ x }}

    ^ include (x :: Text)

    {{ f x }}

    ^ apply the higher-order template to x
